From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:54:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] GS6 patch A: the ground battle's clouds turned on the
 graphics chip (M_CloudTurned), -TheaterSkyChip=0 for the old way

LaySky lays AirSky::Chip's table in a float picture and makes one mesh, once (a puff's room a slot, the painter's
triangles); M_CloudTurned's Custom node runs Battle/AirSkyChip.inl where the points are placed, every frame, for the
eye as it is then. DrawSky only carries the mesh with the wind and, when the puffs' order goes stale, lays the table
again and sends it. The rooms stay, unchanged, for -TheaterSkyChip=0 or a missing material. Tools/build_content.py:
build_cloud_turned (TC_REBUILD=M_CloudTurned), placed in the list away from its tail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L4rhyzzCJpbk7hzRiikzLD
